preConditionHook:
// BUYERS IN CONTROL, MEASURED IN PRICE: the recent up-legs are longer than the
// recent down-legs that separate them. Grimes's trend asymmetry (G01-04), the
// claim Chapter 2's four trades and Chapter 3's trend structure both build on.
// Short is the mirror -- the down-legs longer than the up-legs.
//
// LEGS ARE PIVOT TO PIVOT. On the long side the pivots must alternate with a
// swing high NEWEST, so in bars-ago counts (the older pivot carries the LARGER
// count) they descend hiB1 < loB1 < hiB2 < loB2, and at numLegs 3 the chain
// continues < hiB3 < loB3. The `numLegs` up-legs are hiPx(k) - loPx(k)
// and the numLegs-1 down-legs between them are hiPx(k+1) - loPx(k). The short
// side is the same pivots read the other way round -- a swing pivot low
// newest, so loB1 < hiB1 < loB2 < hiB2 -- where the same hiPx(k) - loPx(k)
// terms are the DOWN-legs and the opposing up-legs are hiPx(k) - loPx(k+1).
// Exactly one of the two orderings can hold on any bar, whichever pivot is
// newer, so the two sides never fire together.
//
// THE COMPARISON IS OF MEANS, WRITTEN AS A PRODUCT to keep it division-free:
// mean(with-trend) > mean(counter) is
// legSum * (numLegs - 1) > oppSum * numLegs, since there are numLegs
// with-trend legs and numLegs - 1 counter legs. At numLegs 2 that is the
// source's "upSum / 2 > downSum / 1".
//
// numLegs IS CAPPED AT 3 BY THE SCAN, which keeps three pivots per series
// (merge decision 14). A larger value never reaches its pivot count and the
// rule never fires; numLegs below 2 is rejected by the same guard, because one
// leg has no counter-leg to compare against. Default 2.
//
// NOT SwingLegLengthAtLeast, which sizes the last two legs in BARS and puts a
// floor on them; this compares up-leg against down-leg in PRICE. The TIME form
// of the same asymmetry is already CorrectionBarsVsTrendLegBars.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS HAND-ROLLED, not SwingHigh(3, ...): Occurrence 3 and
// beyond is UNMEASURED in the register and numLegs 3 needs a third pivot.
// MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min): the pivot
// bar is AT OR BEYOND the `strength` OLDER bars and STRICTLY BEYOND the
// `strength` NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER kk the NEWER
// bar, so the strict half is the kk < jj loop; the confirmation lag is exactly
// `strength` bars, so jj starts there; candidate offsets run 0..Length-1
// inclusive so jj stops at maxBarsBack - 1, while the neighbourhood test
// reaches `strength` bars PAST the window -- deepest bar touched
// maxBarsBack - 1 + strength; scanning newest-first and recording the first
// three hits reproduces Occurrence 1, 2, 3; the comparisons carry the
// 2.22e-12 relational tolerance; the low side's tie sense is the mirror of the
// measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingHigh exists, so plain EL governs.
// Written WITHOUT break, matching the twin statement for statement, and the
// < 3 guards stop a fourth pivot being recorded.
//
// THE SENTINEL IS GUARDED BY THE COUNTS (nHiPiv / nLoPiv reaching numLegs),
// never by a price test: -1.00 and 0.00 are legitimate prices in a
// back-adjusted series. The bar slots carry -1 too, and they are bar indices,
// where -1 is safe.
//
// Every scratch value that must survive the bar is a localVariables entry
// rather than a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement; the loop counters and per-candidate flags are block-scoped.
//
// Deepest bar touched: maxBarsBack - 1 + strength.
pivS = (int)strength;
pivW = (int)maxBarsBack;
nHiPiv = 0;
nLoPiv = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiPx3 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loPx3 = -1.0;
hiB1 = -1.0;
hiB2 = -1.0;
hiB3 = -1.0;
loB1 = -1.0;
loB2 = -1.0;
loB3 = -1.0;
for (int jj = pivS; jj <= pivW - 1; ++jj) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int kk = jj - pivS; kk < jj; ++kk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + pivS; ++kk) {
        if (!el_ge(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHiPiv < 3) {
        nHiPiv = nHiPiv + 1;
        if (nHiPiv == 1) { hiPx1 = high[jj]; hiB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 2) { hiPx2 = high[jj]; hiB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nHiPiv == 3) { hiPx3 = high[jj]; hiB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLoPiv < 3) {
        nLoPiv = nLoPiv + 1;
        if (nLoPiv == 1) { loPx1 = low[jj]; loB1 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 2) { loPx2 = low[jj]; loB2 = (double)jj; }
        if (nLoPiv == 3) { loPx3 = low[jj]; loB3 = (double)jj; }
    }
}
legSum = (hiPx1 - loPx1) + (hiPx2 - loPx2);
oppUp = hiPx2 - loPx1;
oppDn = hiPx1 - loPx2;
ordUp = el_lt(hiB1, loB1) && el_lt(loB1, hiB2) && el_lt(hiB2, loB2);
ordDn = el_lt(loB1, hiB1) && el_lt(hiB1, loB2) && el_lt(loB2, hiB2);
if (el_ge(numLegs, 3.0)) {
    legSum = legSum + (hiPx3 - loPx3);
    oppUp = oppUp + (hiPx3 - loPx2);
    oppDn = oppDn + (hiPx2 - loPx3);
    ordUp = ordUp && el_lt(loB2, hiB3) && el_lt(hiB3, loB3);
    ordDn = ordDn && el_lt(hiB2, loB3) && el_lt(loB3, hiB3);
}
haveLegs = el_ge(numLegs, 2.0) && el_ge((double)nHiPiv, numLegs) && el_ge((double)nLoPiv, numLegs);
haveUp = haveLegs && ordUp;
haveDn = haveLegs && ordDn;
